  "definition": "A bilateral barbell power lift beginning at mid-thigh, loading to just above the knees, accelerating through triple extension, pulling under, receiving overhead above full-squat depth, and recovering to standing. Ordered phases preserve both the yielding loading and catch motions and the produced overhead actions. Weakley et al. directly own the hang start, loading phase, triple-extension sequence, delayed elbow bend, overhead power receive, and Power classification, while Geisler et al. support measured lower-body, trapezius, and trunk activity. Neither study measures the declared shoulder and scapular actions or a complete muscle hierarchy. Shoulder flexion and abduction, scapular upward rotation and posterior tilt, elbow extension, and their categorical upper-body roles are therefore explicit transfers from Ackland et al., Holzbaur et al., and Seth et al., not hang-power-snatch-specific magnitude rankings. The 45-pound, 20-kilogram, and three-repetition seeds are product defaults rather than source prescriptions. Floor starts, full-squat catches, and snatch pulls without an overhead receive remain outside this family.",
