      "execution": {
        "startingPosition": "Stand with the bar at mid-thigh using a wide overhand snatch grip, straight elbows, and a rigid trunk.",
        "movement": "Lower the bar to just above the knees, then rapidly extend the hips, knees, and ankles, elevate the shoulders, and bend the elbows only after that extension to pull under.",
        "endpoint": "Receive the bar overhead in a power quarter squat with fully straight elbows and the hip crease above the knees.",
        "returnPhase": "Stand from the catch, then lower the bar under control to mid-thigh before the next repetition.",
        "controlledJoints": "Control hip, knee, and ankle flexion during loading and receiving while keeping the bar close.",
        "supportAndPosture": "Brace the trunk and maintain the wide two-hand grip without external support.",
        "disqualifyingCompensations": ["Bending the elbows before triple extension changes the reviewed pull sequence.", "Receiving below power depth changes the exercise into a full hang snatch.", "Starting from the floor changes the exercise into a floor power snatch."]
